; Control code 7: print the name of the first object with an article
;
; Sets the article flag ($B703) and prints the name of the first object of the
; command ($B6E8). If $B6FE (first noun is a location) is set it is a location
; id and its name is found with #R$71D5, otherwise an object with #R$71E2; the
; name is printed by #R$7434. The second entry leaves the article flag as the
; caller set it (used by #R$712B). Shares the lookup in #R$73C2.
; .
; The printer calls this handler with IX at the code byte. Return Z when there
; is nothing to print; NZ with a word token in DE and the printer prints it.
;
; O:A 0
; O:F Z
@label=PrintFirstObjectName
c$73AF LD A,$01      ;
 $73B1 LD ($B703),A  ; PhraseMode: with article
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$712B.
@label=PrintFirstObjectNameAsIs
*$73B4 LD A,($B6FE)  ; Noun1Kind
 $73B7 AND A         ;
 $73B8 LD A,($B6E8)  ; FirstObject
 $73BB JR $73CE      ;
